      "comment": "I checked whether the plan surveyed the existing tree evidence and explained its relevance to Michael's migration question. The response mentions Patrick Sheahan's 1875 land purchase in Schuylkill County, citing Deed Book 42, p. 118, but does not clearly integrate this existing evidence into the initial survey's reasoning. Patrick's purchase establishes that Michael's sibling had a connection to the destination county seven years before Michael's documented arrival, supporting chain migration as a hypothesis worth investigating. The plan should explicitly connect this sourced deed to the migration question before proposing new searches. The new record selections and sequencing are otherwise sound."
    },
